    <section id="architecture" class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="card-title-group">
          <span class="card-title">🏗️ How This API Works in Workshops 8 &amp; 9</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
          In CASA0017, you build client-side web applications (such as Leaflet maps or data dashboards) that consume spatial databases through a REST API. This server bridges your web browser and the MySQL database:
        </p>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 1rem;">
            <div style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">1. Browser Request</div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
              Your client script uses JavaScript <code>fetch()</code> or <code>$.getJSON()</code> to call an API endpoint with coordinates or camera parameters.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 1rem;">
            <div style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">2. Spatial SQL Query</div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
              The server runs <code>DISTANCE(points, POINT(lon, lat)) &lt;= radius</code> in MySQL to find points inside the circle in kilometers.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 1rem;">
            <div style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--success); margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">3. JSON Response &amp; Map</div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
              The server returns JSON arrays. Your web app loops over the records to plot Leaflet markers and popups on the map.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #e0f2fe; border-left: 4px solid var(--primary); padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9rem;">
          <b>📐 Great-Circle Distance Function:</b> Distance calculation uses the custom MySQL function:<br>
          <code style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #0369a1;">CREATE FUNCTION distance(a POINT, b POINT) RETURNS double DETERMINISTIC RETURN ifnull(acos(sin(X(a)) * sin(X(b)) + cos(X(a)) * cos(X(b)) * cos(Y(b) - Y(a))) * 6380, 0)</code>
          <br><span style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #64748b;">(Multiplies by 6380 km, representing the mean radius of the Earth).</span>
        </div>
      </div>
